WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:05.773
After 177 episodes, "The Walking Dead" has
finally come to a conclusion.

00:00:05.773 --> 00:00:07.711
Well, sort of.

00:00:07.711 --> 00:00:09.155
Are zombies evolving?

00:00:09.155 --> 00:00:11.470
Will Michonne ever end up finding Rick?

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:16.160
Fans definitely have questions about plenty
of loose ends, and we're here to explore the

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.062
most pressing of them.

00:00:18.164 --> 00:00:22.740
When "The Walking Dead" premiered on Halloween
of 2010, we were introduced to Rick Grimes,

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:25.870
who woke up from a coma in the middle of a
zombie apocalypse.

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:31.150
The fast-paced horror of that episode gave
way to years of post-apocalyptic social drama,

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.360
spending practically no time exploring what
happened to cause the outbreak.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:38.310
There have been plenty of hints as to what
initially caused the outbreak.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:42.730
For instance, an episode of "Tales of the
Walking Dead" set in the future notes that

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:46.960
scientists eventually learn that the virus
was created in a French laboratory.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:51.480
Likewise, we've seen something of the catastrophic
early days of the infestation through the

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:56.239
underrated spin-off "The Walking Dead: World
Beyond" as several children experienced some

00:00:56.239 --> 00:01:00.260
of their earliest memories of losing their
parents to the sudden influx of undead.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:04.720
Yet, there are still plenty of questions around
what exactly caused the outbreak, and it's

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.520
hard to say if the franchise is ever going
to address them.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:12.330
In many ways, the beauty of "The Walking Dead"
is that we don't actually need to know what

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:15.000
happened — but we can't help but be curious.

00:01:15.895 --> 00:01:20.144
Rick's farewell to "The Walking Dead" series
in the 9th season is epic.

00:01:20.144 --> 00:01:24.341
Despite hallucinating and being near death,
he manages to divert a horde of undead away

00:01:24.341 --> 00:01:25.799
from his friends and family.

00:01:25.799 --> 00:01:30.520
When an explosion takes out a mass of the
walkers, it seems certain that Rick has met

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.340
his demise, as he is nowhere to be found afterward.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:37.049
Enter Jadis, who we meet in the 7th season
as the leader of the Scavengers.

00:01:37.049 --> 00:01:41.320
Her time with the group shows her to be an
enigmatic and puzzling character, and she

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:44.020
ultimately leaves to join the militaristic
CRM.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:48.380
When we see her again in "The Walking Dead:
World Beyond," she makes veiled references

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:52.170
that could easily prove she knows more about
Rick's whereabouts than anyone.

00:01:52.601 --> 00:01:54.780
"And I created a ticket to get into the Civic
Republic.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.619
I gave the CRM something very valuable."

00:01:57.619 --> 00:02:02.470
Jadis saves Rick with the help of a helicopter,
and then the series jumps six years into the

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:06.610
future, where Michonne writes diary entries
to her presumably late husband.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:11.390
However, in the 10th season, Michonne finds
Rick's boots and an old iPhone with her and

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:16.690
Judith's faces carved onto its surface, and
she realizes that Rick is very likely still

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:19.050
alive, leading her to head off to find him.

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:22.840
In the finale, it seems more likely than ever
that we're eventually going to figure out

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:26.080
what Rick has been up to — but currently
it's still a mystery.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:29.940
Since Rick has always been the face of the
series, it goes without saying that his fate

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:33.637
is possibly the most pressing question fans
have.

00:02:33.637 --> 00:02:38.489
"The Walking Dead" is well-known for introducing
epic big bads, from the Governor to Negan

00:02:38.489 --> 00:02:39.980
to Alpha and the Whisperers.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:46.020
For the 11th season, the major enemy is the
seemingly non-violent Pamela Milton, who "disappears"

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.020
countless Commonwealth citizens that prove
problematic to her.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:54.150
Aiding her is her hateful and spoiled son
Sebastian as well as Lance Hornsby, a politician

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:58.900
who constantly lies to get people on his side
only to revoke his support in crucial moments

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:03.519
to colonize the outlying communities in some
sort of manifest destiny plan that we may

00:03:03.519 --> 00:03:05.580
never see the full extent of.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:10.990
Sebastian and Lance both meet satisfying deaths,
and Pamela gets captured after her evil actions

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:16.739
are made known to the citizens of The Commonwealth,
but maybe that's not the last we'll see of Pamela.

00:03:17.152 --> 00:03:21.879
Though there are plenty of surprises with
the undead in the early seasons of the show,

00:03:21.879 --> 00:03:25.980
over time, they become more of a static background
threat that could occasionally leap forward

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:29.069
and take loved ones if you aren't constantly
alert.

00:03:29.069 --> 00:03:33.500
Living humans remain the most unpredictable
threat in the post-apocalypse, while the undead

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:35.550
stick to traveling in herds and feeding.

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:40.269
This final season changes that, and the danger
of the hordes grows exponentially.

00:03:40.269 --> 00:03:44.730
Through several episodes, different characters
notice odd developments with the zombies,

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:48.140
surprised to find them in places that they
shouldn't have been able to go, casually dropping

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:52.960
hints to viewers that the undead might be
evolving into a greater threat than ever before.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:57.230
When a group takes refuge in an abandoned
township, they see the extent of this as a

00:03:57.230 --> 00:04:01.666
walker not only scales a wall but opens a
door simply by using the handle.

00:04:01.666 --> 00:04:04.309
"When did the dead use frickin door knobs?"

00:04:04.309 --> 00:04:08.970
Previously, zombies could only bust through
barriers, but using deductive skills was not

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.549
a thing they could pull off.

00:04:10.549 --> 00:04:14.489
During the attack on the Commonwealth, we
see more of them coming over fences and walls,

00:04:14.489 --> 00:04:17.633
demonstrating again that the undead are getting
smarter.

00:04:18.774 --> 00:04:22.690
From the beginning of "The Walking Dead" up
to his death in the 8th season, Carl Grimes

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:25.780
played a major role as his father Rick's right-hand
man.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:29.860
When Rick teetered on the edge, nearly giving
in to his dark side, Carl was able to call

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:34.718
him back, pointing out that his own belief
system should prevent him from crossing those lines.

00:04:34.718 --> 00:04:39.870
In that way, the next generation has always
played a huge role in the morality of the franchise.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:45.660
With Rick, Michonne, and Carl all gone, Judith
becomes a major character over the last few seasons.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:50.410
Showing the same determination and heroism
as her parents, Judith is able to defend the

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:55.310
other children but also takes part in major
events while inspiring the adults around her

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:58.041
to keep their eyes on the prize during conflicts.

00:04:58.041 --> 00:05:00.482
"What we're doing could help everyone.

00:05:00.482 --> 00:05:02.949
Not just us but maybe everybody everywhere."

00:05:02.949 --> 00:05:07.580
Though we almost lose her in the finale due
to a gunshot wound, Judith survives, leading

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:10.500
us to wonder where she and the other children
will go from here.

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:16.080
We have no idea where Rick has been over the
last several years, though the hints dropped

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.949
in the finale suggest he's probably in need
of some help.

00:05:18.949 --> 00:05:23.650
We see him decked out in a CRM jacket, stuck
at a riverbank, dismayed by the number of

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:26.620
undead stuck in the mud and snapping at his
feet.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:30.930
He throws his backpack on a boat to keep it
from being confiscated, leaving a trail for

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:34.060
Michonne to find, as a voice through a loudspeaker
warns him,

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:36.490
"There is no escape for the living."

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:40.340
If there is one thing we have seen time and
again in this series, it's Michonne pulling

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:42.880
off superhuman feats of bravery.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:46.750
As Rick surrenders to his captors, images
are intercut with Michonne, who has never

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:48.210
stopped searching for him.

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:52.940
Alone and surrounded by the horde, she continues
on, hacking away at the undead with her trusty

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:56.680
blade and riding an armored horse into battle
in search of her love.

00:05:56.680 --> 00:06:01.360
"Rick and Michonne" will no doubt see a reunion
between the two, even if only through memories

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:05.810
and flashbacks, but it's not guaranteed that
Michonne and Rick will make it to safety.

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:09.690
With Richonne fans across the globe holding
their breaths, we're hoping to get some answers

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:11.513
in 2023.

00:06:12.613 --> 00:06:17.240
This season spends a lot of time delving into
the animosity between long-time fan favorite

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:22.150
Maggie Greene and the villain turned antihero
Negan, who murdered her husband Glenn during

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:24.940
his time as the ruthless leader of the Saviors.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:29.139
Understandably, Maggie is still upset about
this, despite Negan's presence as a helpful

00:06:29.139 --> 00:06:31.353
member of the Alexandria community.

00:06:31.353 --> 00:06:37.835
"Killing you, it's always on my mind."

00:06:37.835 --> 00:06:42.300
Now married and soon to be a father, Negan
is wracked with guilt over what he's done

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:46.199
and attempts to sacrifice himself to a firing
squad to save the others.

00:06:46.199 --> 00:06:50.230
But, to Negan's shock, he gets rescued by
Ezekiel and other members of the community

00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:52.120
stepping up around him and Annie.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:56.789
After that, he apologizes to Maggie for the
first time, telling her that it took all of

00:06:56.789 --> 00:07:00.280
the horrors they've been through for him to
fully understand what he had taken from her.

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:09.810
"I am so sorry for what I took from you and
what I took from your son."

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:14.110
Though she tells him she can't forgive him,
she admits that she's ready to move forward,

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:17.039
which will open the door for their pending
spin-off, "Dead City."

00:07:17.039 --> 00:07:19.870
However, we still don't know how they end
up in New York.

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:25.470
After Rick and Michonne leave the series,
Daryl makes a seamless transition into a central

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:30.440
role, where he spends more time with the community,
helps to raise Judith, and even works for

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:32.669
Mercer as one of the Commonwealth's soldiers.

00:07:32.669 --> 00:07:36.750
His dedication to the community has been clear
since the early days and he's always been

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:40.550
a true friend to both Rick and Michonne during
their time as leaders.

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:44.771
More so than almost anyone else, he and Carol
have remained vital characters, surprising

00:07:44.771 --> 00:07:47.650
us countless times by jumping in and saving
the day.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:52.020
The finale sees Daryl spending most of his
time trying to keep Judith alive as the horde

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:54.159
overruns the streets of the Commonwealth.

00:07:54.159 --> 00:07:58.490
In her delirious state upon waking up, Judith
admits to Daryl that Michonne is on a quest

00:07:58.490 --> 00:07:59.490
to find Rick.

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:02.919
Surprised to hear that his friends are still
alive, he doesn't make any immediate moves

00:08:02.919 --> 00:08:06.460
until we cut to the One Year Later segment
that ends the series.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:10.704
Daryl says a touching goodbye to Carol while
preparing to head off on his own journey.

00:08:10.704 --> 00:08:12.370
Where is he going?

00:08:12.547 --> 00:08:15.590
We're not sure, but we're guessing that Rick
and Michonne are at the end of that path.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:20.810
The ending of "The Walking Dead" was pretty
great overall, but the series couldn't fully

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:24.800
manage to grant adequate screen time to its
countless amazing characters.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:28.090
Though arcs for many characters wrapped up
or at least put them on the path to their

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:30.960
next adventure, plenty of others struggled
to find a resolution.

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:36.150
The Commonwealth is now the home of many recurring
characters, from sisters Connie and Kelly

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:41.010
to King Ezekiel himself, and these are all
people we're dying to see more of.

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:44.750
Since Magna's group first appeared in the
9th season, they've counterbalanced the loss

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:49.250
of major cast members by repeatedly proving
their survival skills are unmatched.

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:53.660
Eugene and Max fought hard for their relative
sense of peace, but are we ever going to see

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:55.430
what Eugene is like as a dad?

00:08:55.842 --> 00:08:58.121
"That there is a video game worth a pre-order."

00:08:58.446 --> 00:09:02.769
Over the years, "The Walking Dead" has been
surprisingly adept at tying up its loose ends

00:09:02.769 --> 00:09:07.870
and viewers seldom lose sight of a major character
or plot thread without some sort of explanation.

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:12.460
However, the people behind the show are only
human, so there are still a handful of questions

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:15.779
left over from the earlier seasons that we've
never quite resolved.

00:09:15.779 --> 00:09:20.470
For instance, way back in the 4th season,
Grady Memorial Hospital was shown to be overrun

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:25.290
by villainous monsters masquerading as healthcare
officials, but after Beth Greene's death,

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:27.330
we never hear about it again.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:31.450
Even though Daryl killed the head of the organization,
we've spent years wondering what happened

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:32.560
to everyone else.

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:36.310
Another question that has fans scratching
their heads is, "What has the Civic Republic

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:37.310
been up to?"

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:40.940
We're pretty sure they have to be aware of
major townships like the Commonwealth.

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:44.620
We've seen their "ends justify the means"
approach up close and personal through the

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:48.950
"The Walking Dead: World Beyond," but their
status as ruthless protectors of humanity

00:09:48.950 --> 00:09:50.570
has always been a bit vague.

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:51.965
We're dying to hear more.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:57.650
With Hilltop destroyed and both Alexandria
and Oceanside having been invaded by Commonwealth

00:09:57.650 --> 00:10:02.470
soldiers, it's harder than ever to understand
what's going on in the outlying communities.

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:06.210
And their fates are even more jeopardized
now that so many of their best and brightest

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:08.880
members are all heading off in different directions.

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:13.520
The benevolent King Ezekiel is unlikely to
ever turn his back on the other communities,

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:15.910
particularly the ones he once found a home
in.

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:20.329
Aaron was uniquely committed to Alexandria,
which means he very well might return to it

00:10:20.329 --> 00:10:22.430
as a leader and usher in a new era.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:26.770
The full status of Oceanside and whether it
will make a comeback is unknown, but we're

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:28.924
looking forward to finding out soon.

